WEBVTT

00:12.180 --> 00:18.030
I believe there are three kinds of
people who make others happy.

00:18.790 --> 00:21.960
This is the I-1 Club!

00:31.090 --> 00:32.669
I! I!

00:32.670 --> 00:34.389
I-1 Club!

00:34.390 --> 00:35.839
I! I!

00:35.840 --> 00:37.559
I-1 Club!

00:37.560 --> 00:39.080
I! I!

00:37.620 --> 00:40.920
There are those who make many
different people happy across the world.

00:39.080 --> 00:40.670
I-1 Club!

00:46.410 --> 00:50.520
Those who make everyone around them happy.

00:51.780 --> 00:52.780
And those

00:54.760 --> 00:57.170
who make only themselves happy.

00:58.530 --> 01:00.249
Harder than anyone!

01:00.250 --> 01:01.539
More beautiful than anyone!

01:01.540 --> 01:03.469
More precise than anyone!

01:03.470 --> 01:06.419
I-1 Club, let's go!

01:06.420 --> 01:07.540
Yeah!

01:07.550 --> 01:10.049
It is the Age of Warring Idols

01:10.050 --> 01:12.050
July 2013 Sendai

01:12.050 --> 01:14.050
- Green Leaves Entertainment
- Green Leaves Entertainment

01:15.910 --> 01:16.910
What?!

01:17.210 --> 01:19.170
You won't be able to
come, starting tomorrow?!

01:19.630 --> 01:21.119
You're betraying me?!

01:21.120 --> 01:23.930
How do you think you've
gotten so successful?

01:24.650 --> 01:26.729
Enough! I don't want to hear it anymore!

01:26.730 --> 01:29.360
Go wherever you want, bitch!

01:35.920 --> 01:38.629
So is Sapphire Reiko-san quitting, then?

01:38.630 --> 01:40.229
I fired her!

01:40.230 --> 01:42.929
Everyone's going on
about Tokyo this, Tokyo that!

01:42.930 --> 01:44.379
It's ridiculous that they think

01:44.380 --> 01:47.129
they can make money
in such a disgusting city!

01:47.130 --> 01:49.960
I hope they get a reality check
and end up selling their bodies!

01:53.580 --> 01:56.590
Well, what are we going to do now?

01:56.980 --> 01:58.869
What do you mean,
"What are we going to do now?"

01:58.870 --> 02:00.770
We just gotta find the next one!

02:02.930 --> 02:03.930
This...

02:03.931 --> 02:06.029
The I-1 Club is great, isn't it?

02:06.030 --> 02:08.649
They're idols who represent Japan,

02:08.650 --> 02:11.879
but they're also supporting the
Japanese entertainment industry.

02:11.880 --> 02:16.029
Even though we're in a
recession, they've got an audience.

02:16.030 --> 02:18.329
All of their singles are
selling in the millions.

02:18.330 --> 02:21.130
People line up outside of their
concerts, hoping somebody will cancel.

02:21.840 --> 02:23.329
Given how well they sell,

02:23.330 --> 02:26.880
I wonder how much President
Shiraki earns from royalties.

02:27.950 --> 02:29.590
This stinks.

02:30.010 --> 02:31.529
It absolutely stinks.

02:31.530 --> 02:33.629
Huh? President, don't you like coffee?

02:33.630 --> 02:34.729
What are you talking about?

02:34.730 --> 02:36.079
I'm talking about <i>this</i>!

02:36.080 --> 02:38.090
It freaking stinks of money!

02:39.440 --> 02:41.329
Matsuda, we're going to do it!

02:41.330 --> 02:43.049
We're going to start making idols!

02:43.050 --> 02:44.139
What?

02:44.140 --> 02:46.579
This is definitely going to work!

02:46.580 --> 02:48.709
We're experiencing a huge
boom in idols! This won't fail!

02:48.710 --> 02:50.709
It'll never work in Sendai.

02:50.710 --> 02:51.979
Shut up!

02:51.980 --> 02:53.729
We'll never know unless we give it a shot!

02:53.730 --> 02:55.529
You're a disgrace to the Date Clan!

02:55.530 --> 02:57.569
But I'm not a warrior...

02:57.570 --> 02:59.129
If I say we do it, we do it!

02:59.130 --> 03:01.669
Go find us some pretty girls, you insect!

03:01.670 --> 03:03.489
What? You mean now?

03:03.490 --> 03:04.589
Yes!

03:04.590 --> 03:07.539
Go find us some golden
eggs—no, golden girls!

03:07.540 --> 03:08.540
Got it?!

03:09.040 --> 03:10.500
This again.

03:11.130 --> 03:15.130
She's always so pushy and irresponsible,
deciding things so frivolously.

03:15.580 --> 03:18.760
That's why our clients keep quitting.

03:23.910 --> 03:26.140
Maybe I'll quit soon, too...

03:26.890 --> 03:28.149
I wanted to watch, too.

03:28.150 --> 03:29.959
You weren't watching?

03:29.960 --> 03:31.229
No.

03:31.230 --> 03:33.020
That's such a waste.

03:31.680 --> 03:33.020
In any case...

03:33.490 --> 03:35.019
Hey, you.

03:35.020 --> 03:38.779
Would you girls like to become idols?

03:38.780 --> 03:42.720
I'm a manager for a talent agency, you see.

03:43.240 --> 03:44.240
My name is...

03:47.680 --> 03:48.920
Right.

03:54.250 --> 03:56.010
- You can be a star!
- You can be a star!

03:54.250 --> 03:56.010
- Large Idol Group
- Large Idol Group

03:54.250 --> 03:56.010
- AUDITION Open!!
- AUDITION Open!!

03:57.230 --> 03:58.830
Sorry to keep you waiting.

04:07.540 --> 04:08.640
E-Excuse me.

04:09.110 --> 04:09.810
Huh?

04:09.811 --> 04:11.270
An idol... would you...

04:13.660 --> 04:16.380
Never mind, it's nothing.

04:29.190 --> 04:32.529
This isn't how I'd imagine idols.

04:32.530 --> 04:34.829
It's important for them to be sexy, too.

04:34.830 --> 04:35.830
Look, over there.

04:39.330 --> 04:40.579
U-Um...

04:40.580 --> 04:42.259
Welcome!

04:42.260 --> 04:46.879
Um, would you, uh... be
interested in becoming an idol?

04:46.880 --> 04:48.029
Huh? What?

04:48.030 --> 04:51.529
Uh, I work for this talent
agency, called Green Leaves...

04:51.530 --> 04:52.809
Hey, buddy.

04:52.810 --> 04:55.129
You've got some guts.

04:55.130 --> 04:57.640
Are you <i>really</i> trying to steal one
of my girls, right outside my store?

04:57.641 --> 04:59.305
No, that's not what I'm...

04:59.306 --> 05:01.379
Why don't we have a little chat inside?

05:01.380 --> 05:03.229
No, you're mistaken, it's not like that!

05:03.230 --> 05:05.780
I know what I see when I see it!

05:06.530 --> 05:08.105
Hey, stop!

05:08.106 --> 05:09.470
It's not like that!

05:08.780 --> 05:09.470
Don't run away!

05:09.471 --> 05:11.290
What an idiot.

05:13.290 --> 05:14.540
- You can be a star!
- You can be a star!

05:13.290 --> 05:14.540
- Large Idol Group
- Large Idol Group

05:13.290 --> 05:14.540
- AUDITION Open!!
- AUDITION Open!!

05:22.020 --> 05:23.670
You're Shimada Mayu, right?

05:25.220 --> 05:28.029
You were an idol until
recently, weren't you?

05:28.030 --> 05:31.099
A lot of girls in our
class know who you are.

05:31.100 --> 05:32.629
Why did you quit?

05:32.630 --> 05:34.310
Did you have trouble with boys?

05:35.150 --> 05:39.650
Did you know? You're known
as the "Fallen Idol" at school.

05:40.010 --> 05:41.779
If you don't explain yourself,

05:41.780 --> 05:44.160
the rumors will only get worse.

05:44.780 --> 05:46.629
It's okay to tell us.

05:46.630 --> 05:48.120
We'll protect you.

05:51.080 --> 05:53.579
I guess she really can't tell us.

05:53.580 --> 05:55.080
It can't be helped, then.

05:56.880 --> 05:58.249
So lame.

05:58.250 --> 05:59.250
Rude.

06:02.320 --> 06:03.339
You're definitely sure?

06:03.340 --> 06:04.340
Yes.

06:04.850 --> 06:07.179
You know, you can't change your mind later.

06:07.180 --> 06:08.949
It's okay.

06:08.950 --> 06:12.329
Besides, why would I quit?

06:12.330 --> 06:14.379
I'd never do that.

06:14.380 --> 06:15.730
Please believe in me.

06:16.180 --> 06:18.849
Well then, here's your entry sheet.

06:18.850 --> 06:20.480
Here, you can have this, too.

06:20.830 --> 06:21.440
Huh?

06:21.441 --> 06:24.289
You should come to our store.

06:24.290 --> 06:26.849
Make sure you ask for me.

06:26.850 --> 06:30.229
Just twenty more
points, and I'll get a raise!

06:30.230 --> 06:31.739
I see...

06:31.740 --> 06:36.750
You know, I've always wanted to be an idol.

06:37.190 --> 06:43.809
I even thought about leaving Sendai
and auditioning for the I-1 Club...

06:43.810 --> 06:47.440
but I'm unable to save
enough money to go to Tokyo.

06:47.870 --> 06:50.889
Come to think of it, I don't have
a winning personality, either.

06:50.890 --> 06:51.760
You're right.

06:51.761 --> 06:52.879
Huh?

06:52.880 --> 06:54.229
Do you really think that?

06:54.230 --> 06:55.549
Do you really think I can't?

06:55.550 --> 06:58.520
No, no, it's not like that.

07:02.280 --> 07:05.240
Name

07:02.760 --> 07:05.270
Hisami Nanami, thirteen years old.

07:07.760 --> 07:10.829
I've been fascinated with performing
arts ever since I was young.

07:10.830 --> 07:15.029
I've taken singing,
dancing and acting lessons.

07:15.030 --> 07:19.370
I'd like to audition to test my abilities.

07:17.790 --> 07:20.040
Hisami Nanami

07:23.960 --> 07:26.180
Hayashida Airi, sixteen years old.

07:26.530 --> 07:29.080
I don't have any confidence, but...

07:27.200 --> 07:28.359
See you later.

07:28.360 --> 07:29.565
Huh? You're going out?

07:29.566 --> 07:31.630
But, I wanted to give it a go.

07:31.631 --> 07:32.805
Yeah, to a friend's.

07:32.806 --> 07:34.550
I've never sung or danced before,

07:34.560 --> 07:37.270
Hayashida Airi

07:34.960 --> 07:36.580
but I look forward to working with you.

07:37.430 --> 07:39.980
Kikuma Kaya, eighteen years old.

07:38.280 --> 07:39.779
You're joking, right?

07:39.780 --> 07:41.300
I can't believe you slapped a customer

07:41.780 --> 07:44.059
just for touching your ass a little.

07:44.060 --> 07:46.930
I decided to audition after
I saw a magazine at work.

07:48.240 --> 07:52.030
Hey! Those boots belong to me, too!

07:52.940 --> 07:55.629
I kind of want to change who I am,

07:55.630 --> 07:57.460
so I wanted to give it a shot.

07:57.830 --> 07:59.280
That's all.

07:57.830 --> 07:59.830
Kikuma Kaya

08:05.230 --> 08:07.950
Here's the girl I scouted.

08:08.340 --> 08:10.970
Okamoto Miyu, seventeen years old.

08:11.700 --> 08:13.755
I'll snatch everyone's
hearts with my pretty aura!

08:13.756 --> 08:15.880
All right. Cast a delicious spell on me.

08:14.680 --> 08:16.455
I'll put a stomach hold on your heart!

08:16.456 --> 08:17.780
Become delicious!

08:17.780 --> 08:18.780
Moe! Moe!

08:17.781 --> 08:20.600
I'm the nurturing, softy
angel, Okamoto Miyu!

08:18.781 --> 08:20.599
Pretty! Pretty!

08:20.600 --> 08:23.600
I will definitely become an idol!

08:20.600 --> 08:23.610
Okamoto Miyu

08:24.240 --> 08:25.539
What do you think?

08:25.540 --> 08:28.279
Her saying of "stomach hold" is weird.

08:28.280 --> 08:29.130
Right...

08:29.130 --> 08:30.130
Well, whatever.

08:30.131 --> 08:31.649
Let's include her.

08:31.650 --> 08:34.599
I scouted two other girls, too.

08:34.600 --> 08:35.600
What?

08:37.300 --> 08:39.580
Nanase Yoshino, sixteen years old.

08:40.800 --> 08:42.189
She looks familiar.

08:42.190 --> 08:44.859
You still have no idea what you're doing!

08:44.860 --> 08:46.819
She's very well-known locally.

08:46.820 --> 08:49.590
She used to be a child
actor, now she's a model.

08:49.830 --> 08:52.129
She's even in some local commercials.

08:52.130 --> 08:57.079
You know, the one that goes,
"Yan-yan-ya-yan, Yanagiyama"...

08:57.080 --> 08:58.600
Oh, that one.

08:59.840 --> 09:02.429
She made it to the end of
the regional group in last year's

09:02.430 --> 09:05.689
Japan Girls' Collection, but
was unable to make it all the way.

09:05.690 --> 09:08.399
Despite her confidence,
she fell flat on her face.

09:08.400 --> 09:10.330
It must've been a disappointment.

09:12.100 --> 09:15.699
Everyone's going on about
Tokyo this, Tokyo that, but there's

09:15.700 --> 09:20.700
no way that someone who can't
win in Sendai, will make it nationally.

09:21.430 --> 09:23.200
You have to win here first.

09:23.930 --> 09:25.930
It's not too late to try after that.

09:28.730 --> 09:30.079
Excuse me...

09:30.080 --> 09:31.979
Well? What do you think?

09:31.980 --> 09:33.960
Do I have to give my answer now?

09:34.330 --> 09:35.349
Excuse me.

09:35.350 --> 09:37.749
I think you already know your answer.

09:37.750 --> 09:38.530
Excuse me!

09:38.530 --> 09:39.380
What?!

09:39.381 --> 09:40.850
You can't smoke here!

09:40.850 --> 09:42.350
Nanase Yoshino

09:41.930 --> 09:46.729
<i>She</i> failed? Just how competitive
is the Japan Girls' Collection?

09:46.730 --> 09:50.230
Regret and defeat make people grow.

09:51.480 --> 09:53.399
There's one more girl...

09:53.400 --> 09:55.830
Katayama Minami, fourteen years old.

09:54.060 --> 09:57.480
The winner is Number
eight, Katayama Minami-san!

09:55.830 --> 09:57.989
I found her at a singing competition.

09:57.990 --> 10:00.239
She's a pretty good singer.

10:00.240 --> 10:02.580
We're going to need at least one of those.

10:01.750 --> 10:03.250
Katayama Minami

10:10.430 --> 10:12.079
There's still no core.

10:12.080 --> 10:12.670
Core?

10:13.100 --> 10:15.969
A center... Someone
to be the center of it all.

10:15.970 --> 10:18.399
Someone with a strong <i>aura</i>.

10:18.400 --> 10:19.779
An aura, huh?

10:19.780 --> 10:21.299
How's your scouting going?

10:21.300 --> 10:22.959
What? But I already found one...

10:22.960 --> 10:24.329
Don't be stupid!

10:24.330 --> 10:26.719
Don't think you've done anything
by bringing me just <i>one</i> girl!

10:26.720 --> 10:27.530
What?

10:27.531 --> 10:29.829
Bring me a diamond in the rough!

10:29.830 --> 10:33.280
Otherwise, I'll hold back your
pay, to cut the next month's costs!

10:33.820 --> 10:36.370
You're killing me...

10:37.760 --> 10:39.249
Cream puffs!

10:39.250 --> 10:40.539
Soft serve ice cream!

10:40.540 --> 10:41.599
Caterpillars!

10:41.600 --> 10:42.600
Maggots!

10:42.330 --> 10:43.370
You maggots!

10:45.880 --> 10:47.180
What was that about?

10:52.680 --> 10:53.799
Hello?

10:53.800 --> 10:55.530
Yeah, I can talk.

10:57.430 --> 10:58.919
Oh, sorry.

10:58.920 --> 11:03.580
I do want to come see your
concert, but I'm busy with work.

11:04.580 --> 11:05.580
Sorry.

11:05.580 --> 11:06.580
Do your best.

11:07.840 --> 11:08.710
Me?

11:08.711 --> 11:11.069
No, I gave up on that long ago.

11:11.070 --> 11:13.110
I haven't even touched my guitar.

11:14.030 --> 11:16.299
Yeah, thanks.

11:16.300 --> 11:17.300
Later.

11:21.180 --> 11:22.330
Dreams, huh?

11:47.000 --> 11:48.770
<i>Maybe I can dream.</i>

12:03.640 --> 12:11.640
The prism of the sky is pointing
towards the place of happiness.

12:15.890 --> 12:23.890
If you find it, please, wait for me there

12:27.930 --> 12:35.930
I'll go as soon as I
wake from my slumber...

12:40.420 --> 12:44.810
I'll go right away...

12:54.040 --> 12:55.040
This girl...

12:58.290 --> 12:59.380
Crap!

13:15.960 --> 13:17.560
I-I'm sorry.

13:18.350 --> 13:19.359
Your aura...

13:19.360 --> 13:20.360
What?

13:20.790 --> 13:23.240
Would you like to become an idol?

13:25.610 --> 13:26.779
I'm sorry.

13:26.780 --> 13:27.929
Wait!

13:27.930 --> 13:31.179
I'm a manager at the
Green Leaves Talent Agency.

13:31.180 --> 13:31.640
What?

13:31.641 --> 13:34.650
We're currently searching for
girls who want to become idols...

13:36.670 --> 13:37.730
I'm sorry!

13:39.090 --> 13:39.880
Wait!

13:39.881 --> 13:42.629
Will you at least take my card?

13:42.630 --> 13:44.980
If you're interested, call...

13:45.930 --> 13:46.979
I'm sorry.

13:46.980 --> 13:49.600
I'm just not interested
in that kind of thing.

13:58.930 --> 13:59.930
Was that...

14:02.570 --> 14:03.570
Mayu!

14:04.430 --> 14:05.599
Sorry I'm late.

14:05.600 --> 14:06.430
Did you wait long?

14:06.431 --> 14:08.129
No, not at all.

14:08.130 --> 14:09.779
Anyway, about this...

14:09.780 --> 14:10.470
Yeah.

14:10.471 --> 14:12.120
I passed the first test.

14:13.720 --> 14:15.130
Congratulations.

14:16.380 --> 14:17.789
Sorry.

14:17.790 --> 14:19.369
Was that inconsiderate?

14:19.370 --> 14:20.979
Not at all.

14:20.980 --> 14:22.189
Definitely not.

14:22.190 --> 14:22.810
Really?

14:22.810 --> 14:23.430
Yeah.

14:23.431 --> 14:27.729
In that case, as long as I'm being
inconsiderate, I need a favor...

14:27.730 --> 14:28.680
What?

14:28.681 --> 14:31.810
You're the only one I can ask.

14:32.230 --> 14:33.230
Huh?

14:40.020 --> 14:41.780
PASS

14:54.790 --> 14:55.870
You can do it

14:54.790 --> 14:55.869
Idol Miyu

15:01.800 --> 15:02.800
- Green Leaves Entertainment
- Idol Auditions

15:05.030 --> 15:06.429
Um, President.

15:06.430 --> 15:07.430
What?

15:07.540 --> 15:10.279
The truth is, I found an amazing girl.

15:10.280 --> 15:11.829
Really? Where's her resume?

15:11.830 --> 15:12.929
I don't have it.

15:12.930 --> 15:13.979
What?

15:13.980 --> 15:16.529
I ran into her at the park the other day.

15:16.530 --> 15:18.929
I tried to talk to her, but she ran away.

15:18.930 --> 15:20.629
Why did you let her run away?!

15:20.630 --> 15:22.179
You're always like this!

15:22.180 --> 15:25.399
You're a weakling who
can't get it up when it counts!

15:25.400 --> 15:26.030
Can't get it...

15:26.031 --> 15:28.979
I figured out the school she goes to,
from her uniform's design...

15:28.980 --> 15:30.530
You did?! Where is it?!

15:31.280 --> 15:32.280
Yes!

15:35.380 --> 15:36.080
Excuse me.

15:36.081 --> 15:37.950
Is this where you're holding the auditions?

15:38.280 --> 15:39.080
You...

15:39.081 --> 15:40.935
Why, if it isn't Shimada Mayu!

15:40.936 --> 15:42.320
What? You know her?

15:46.480 --> 15:48.130
Did you come to audition?

15:48.600 --> 15:51.430
No, I'm just here with my friend.

15:52.200 --> 15:54.469
I can go home now, right?

15:54.470 --> 15:56.119
What? But...

15:56.120 --> 15:57.549
You'll be fine.

15:57.550 --> 15:59.529
You've practiced so much.

15:59.530 --> 16:00.530
Okay...

16:00.980 --> 16:02.080
Good luck.

16:03.020 --> 16:05.109
That's her! The one who ran away from me...

16:05.110 --> 16:06.080
What did you say?!

16:06.081 --> 16:07.129
Go after her!

16:07.130 --> 16:08.749
Bring her back here!

16:08.750 --> 16:09.750
Yes, ma'am!

16:19.580 --> 16:20.580
That's...

16:21.500 --> 16:22.580
Wait.

16:23.100 --> 16:24.100
Listen...

16:24.400 --> 16:25.979
You understand now, don't you?

16:25.980 --> 16:28.559
I really am a manager at a talent agency,

16:28.560 --> 16:30.319
and I really was trying to scout...

16:30.320 --> 16:32.129
I told you I'm not interested.

16:32.130 --> 16:33.929
Listen to me for a minute.

16:33.930 --> 16:35.729
If I let you leave, the president will...

16:35.730 --> 16:37.580
That's not my problem.

16:40.520 --> 16:42.019
Please, drop it already!

16:42.020 --> 16:44.649
Will you at least audition?

16:44.650 --> 16:45.650
No.

16:47.300 --> 16:48.900
She escaped again.

16:49.480 --> 16:50.879
Shimada Mayu...

16:50.880 --> 16:52.179
She's grown.

16:52.180 --> 16:54.399
Um... Do you know her?

16:54.400 --> 16:55.340
Huh?

16:55.341 --> 16:56.629
You don't know who she is?

16:56.630 --> 16:57.130
Nope.

16:57.131 --> 16:59.329
How long have you been in
the entertainment business?!

16:59.330 --> 17:00.879
One year and three months.

17:00.880 --> 17:04.179
You may be an insect on the bottom
rung of the entertainment industry,

17:04.180 --> 17:06.229
but you should still know that!

17:06.230 --> 17:07.789
You don't need to be so harsh...

17:07.790 --> 17:10.039
She's a first generation
member of the I-1 Club

17:10.040 --> 17:12.929
and former center, Shimada Mayu!

17:12.930 --> 17:13.930
What?!

17:14.960 --> 17:19.029
To say she was the reason the originally bland I-1
Club was pushed to the top of the idol world...

17:19.030 --> 17:22.349
no, to the top of the entertainment world,

17:22.350 --> 17:23.810
wouldn't be an exaggeration.

17:24.880 --> 17:26.830
They had finally made it to the big time.

17:27.250 --> 17:28.829
It was immediately after that...

17:28.830 --> 17:32.479
She lost a battle for the
center, and suddenly graduated.

17:32.480 --> 17:34.580
Her fans and the media
had a field day with it.

17:35.770 --> 17:38.829
Her disappearance was shrouded in mystery,

17:38.830 --> 17:41.330
but I had no idea she was here.

17:42.560 --> 17:46.929
If you had your eye on her,
you're not completely blind.

17:46.930 --> 17:48.129
Is that right?

17:48.130 --> 17:49.729
That's not a compliment.

17:49.730 --> 17:52.679
Until you catch her, you're still
more worthless than a maggot.

17:52.680 --> 17:54.090
I see...

18:04.380 --> 18:06.350
What was she doing here?

18:08.600 --> 18:12.110
Well, the auditions will now begin.

18:15.510 --> 18:16.930
Good work.

18:18.580 --> 18:20.990
Before you go, I have one more question.

18:21.750 --> 18:23.540
Are you virgins?

18:25.500 --> 18:27.750
So, what do you think?

18:28.040 --> 18:29.379
Who are you going to let pass?

18:29.380 --> 18:30.479
They all pass.

18:30.480 --> 18:31.200
What?!

18:31.201 --> 18:34.479
We can't form a group without
at least this many girls, after all.

18:34.480 --> 18:35.829
Yes, but...

18:35.830 --> 18:38.029
Well, that's not the only reason.

18:38.030 --> 18:40.560
As a parasite, though, I'm
sure you don't understand.

18:40.930 --> 18:41.930
I see...

18:42.310 --> 18:45.439
Matsuda, what do you think an idol <i>is</i>?

18:45.440 --> 18:47.009
What? Who knows?

18:47.010 --> 18:48.529
They're stories.

18:48.530 --> 18:49.679
Stories?

18:49.680 --> 18:51.900
Stories represent possibilities.

18:52.290 --> 18:55.400
Those girls are full of possibilities.

18:55.730 --> 18:57.819
Is that the case?

18:57.820 --> 19:00.160
But we're missing one.

19:01.330 --> 19:04.660
These six girls don't smell like money.

19:06.710 --> 19:08.920
<i>I really do need her after all.</i>

19:09.430 --> 19:12.670
Excuse me, but it's time to leave.

19:13.030 --> 19:15.480
Hey! You can't smoke in here!

19:16.030 --> 19:17.479
I told you!

19:17.480 --> 19:18.030
Huh?

19:18.031 --> 19:20.829
I'm sorry. I'll scold him later.

19:20.830 --> 19:21.830
What?!

19:23.180 --> 19:24.680
- [Former I-1<b>] </b>Where is Shimada Mayu now? <b>[</b>Whereabouts unknown<b>]
- Where is she now?</b>

19:23.180 --> 19:24.679
2nd post get

19:24.680 --> 19:25.719
She was the cancer of I-1

19:24.680 --> 19:25.260
They were right to get rid
of her Management was right lol

19:24.680 --> 19:25.390
I heard she demanded President Shiraki

19:24.680 --> 19:25.430
give her special treatment

19:25.930 --> 19:25.968
How did she get that idea...

19:26.180 --> 19:26.218
Shimada is a shitty bitch lololololololol

19:27.140 --> 19:27.178
She disappeared with a guy

19:27.140 --> 19:27.178
Maybe she's pregnant now lolololol

19:32.320 --> 19:33.440
So, this is it...

19:33.440 --> 19:34.950
We'll Show You Everything!!

19:34.950 --> 19:36.990
Thank you.

19:34.950 --> 19:37.450
We Buy High
Nationally Popular
Artist CDs

19:38.621 --> 19:38.740
We Buy High
Nationally Popular
Artist CDs

19:40.451 --> 19:42.450
Used CDs and Records

19:42.450 --> 19:46.159
Well? Did "I-1 Club: We'll
Show You Everything!!" come in?

19:46.160 --> 19:49.039
Yeah. That customer just bought it.

19:49.040 --> 19:50.040
What?!

20:09.270 --> 20:10.270
Mayu.

20:10.980 --> 20:11.980
Oh...

20:12.480 --> 20:13.570
How did it go?

20:15.280 --> 20:16.150
I passed!

20:16.150 --> 20:17.150
That's great!

20:17.150 --> 20:18.070
I'm so glad!

20:18.070 --> 20:18.860
Thanks!

20:18.861 --> 20:20.739
I'm really happy for you.

20:20.740 --> 20:22.829
You seem really happy, too.

20:22.830 --> 20:24.409
It's all thanks to you, Mayu.

20:24.410 --> 20:27.409
If you hadn't helped me
train, I wouldn't have passed.

20:27.410 --> 20:28.869
That's not true.

20:28.870 --> 20:30.250
It is true.

20:30.630 --> 20:33.959
<i>No, you need to hold your
mic in front of your mouth.</i>

20:33.960 --> 20:35.010
<i>O-Okay.</i>

20:35.420 --> 20:36.719
<i>One more time.</i>

20:36.720 --> 20:37.720
<i>Okay.</i>

20:38.840 --> 20:43.469
<i>Because the night is cold, tomorrow...</i>

20:43.470 --> 20:45.769
<i>The mic is bothering me
so much that I can't sing!</i>

20:45.770 --> 20:47.560
<i>Can I see that?</i>

20:47.980 --> 20:51.099
<i>Remember this distance between
your mouth and the mic.</i>

20:51.100 --> 20:52.519
<i>Huh.</i>

20:52.520 --> 20:53.730
<i>Give it a try.</i>

20:57.440 --> 21:01.280
<i>Because the night is cold...</i>

21:01.870 --> 21:05.659
I didn't really sing that well, though.

21:05.660 --> 21:06.580
I see...

21:06.581 --> 21:09.289
Really though, thank you so much.

21:09.290 --> 21:10.540
It's fine.

21:11.290 --> 21:13.790
Anyway, I was thinking...

21:14.130 --> 21:15.130
What?

21:15.750 --> 21:17.340
Well...

21:17.840 --> 21:19.930
You should audition, too.

21:22.180 --> 21:23.969
Ah, sorry.

21:23.970 --> 21:24.550
Huh?

21:24.551 --> 21:26.389
Don't worry about it.

21:26.390 --> 21:27.390
But...

21:27.890 --> 21:30.189
Let me thank you by
treating you to something.

21:30.190 --> 21:31.599
Let's go to Large Boy.

21:31.600 --> 21:32.600
Okay.

21:36.010 --> 21:41.779
Once again, I'm the company's
president and producer, Tange Junko.

21:41.780 --> 21:44.829
And this is your manager...

21:44.830 --> 21:46.429
I'm Matsuda Kohei.

21:46.430 --> 21:48.930
Feel free to use him like a dirty, old rag.

21:50.780 --> 21:51.950
Moving on...

21:53.530 --> 21:55.429
Wake... up...

21:55.430 --> 21:57.029
Wake Up, Girls!

21:57.030 --> 21:59.229
This is the name of your group.

21:59.230 --> 22:00.789
What does it mean?

22:00.790 --> 22:02.879
Rise and shine, little girls?

22:02.880 --> 22:04.529
It's "WUG" for short.

22:03.470 --> 22:06.099
Goal

22:04.530 --> 22:07.720
There was once an English duo called Wham!

22:06.100 --> 22:06.220
- Red vs. White
- Concert

22:09.470 --> 22:17.470
Goal

22:09.470 --> 22:10.660
Red vs.
White

22:10.290 --> 22:11.430
Well, whatever.

22:10.661 --> 22:11.849
Concert

22:11.890 --> 22:14.219
We'll be ambitiously aiming
for the Red vs White Concert!

22:11.931 --> 22:13.850
- Red vs. White
- Concert

22:14.220 --> 22:17.439
Until then, you'll be
working your butts off.

22:14.481 --> 22:14.600
Red vs.
White

22:17.440 --> 22:21.979
Let's celebrate the formation
of Wake Up, Girls! with a drink.

22:21.980 --> 22:23.730
Cheers!

22:24.610 --> 22:25.490
Hayashida-san.

22:25.490 --> 22:26.490
Yes?

22:26.800 --> 22:29.129
How's Shimada-san doing?

22:29.130 --> 22:29.680
What?

22:29.681 --> 22:33.549
Hey, you, bring Shimada Mayu here with you.

22:33.550 --> 22:34.959
Do whatever it takes.

22:34.960 --> 22:37.709
President, I'll do something about her.

22:37.710 --> 22:38.749
Will <i>you</i> be enough?

22:38.750 --> 22:40.129
Shimada Mayu?

22:40.130 --> 22:41.679
Do you mean <i>that</i> Shimada Mayu?

22:41.680 --> 22:42.260
That's right.

22:42.261 --> 22:43.329
Wow.

22:43.330 --> 22:44.659
Shimada Mayu?

22:44.660 --> 22:46.849
She was an idol in the I-1 Club.

22:46.850 --> 22:50.239
Is it because she was in the I-1 Club?

22:50.240 --> 22:51.429
Of course.

22:51.430 --> 22:54.310
She's the last piece of the group.

22:54.510 --> 22:57.279
Then, does this mean
we're not fully formed yet?

22:57.280 --> 23:01.030
Well... We'll start with
this and wait for her.

23:02.020 --> 23:03.020
But...

23:03.430 --> 23:05.000
Hey, give me one.

23:03.730 --> 23:05.900
You shouldn't get your hopes up.

23:05.000 --> 23:05.900
Sure.

23:05.901 --> 23:07.180
What do you mean?

23:08.020 --> 23:10.979
I invited Mayu to the
audition, but she refused.

23:10.980 --> 23:11.980
What is this?

23:12.470 --> 23:14.030
This is good.

23:14.660 --> 23:16.910
Will you let us talk to her?

23:15.480 --> 23:17.680
This is great. What flavor is this?

23:17.681 --> 23:20.430
Sure, but it won't work.

23:18.280 --> 23:19.330
It's pizza flavor.

23:19.830 --> 23:20.930
Huh.

23:20.931 --> 23:24.669
Idols are something that
causes pain, for Mayu.

23:24.670 --> 23:26.550
I'm entirely prepared to be rejected.

23:26.890 --> 23:27.730
What?

23:27.731 --> 23:30.830
I have nothing to lose.
I just want to ask her one more time.

23:32.000 --> 23:33.549
What should I do?

23:33.550 --> 23:35.810
Good work today!

23:36.090 --> 23:38.260
I'm finally an idol!

23:38.780 --> 23:40.829
I can't stop shaking!

23:40.830 --> 23:43.179
I hope we'll get to sing a lot.

23:43.180 --> 23:46.649
You'll be made to sing
until your throat collapses.

23:46.650 --> 23:47.390
Wow...

23:47.391 --> 23:48.879
I don't want that...

23:48.880 --> 23:51.979
In that case, you should
train, so that doesn't happen.

23:51.980 --> 23:53.629
You're confident, aren't you?

23:53.630 --> 23:55.049
Of course I am.

23:55.050 --> 23:58.479
Becoming an idol is just
a stepping stone for me.

23:58.480 --> 24:00.980
I have a much more impressive goal.

24:01.420 --> 24:02.829
You're awfully ambitious.

24:02.830 --> 24:05.730
Anyway, leader, I look
forward to working with you.

24:06.780 --> 24:08.299
Why me?

24:08.300 --> 24:11.429
You have experience in
the entertainment industry.

24:11.430 --> 24:12.829
You're dependable.

24:12.830 --> 24:15.099
I haven't made it past
the local scene, though.

24:15.100 --> 24:18.159
If Shimada Mayu joined
us, that would be amazing.

24:18.160 --> 24:21.229
We could end up being really popular.

24:21.230 --> 24:22.379
You think so?

24:22.380 --> 24:24.559
I hope she'll join.

24:24.560 --> 24:25.560
Huh?

24:27.280 --> 24:28.110
This is...

24:28.111 --> 24:29.440
Huh? What, what, what?

24:30.820 --> 24:32.700
What?!

24:40.610 --> 24:42.169
Thanks for meeting me.

24:42.170 --> 24:45.129
I only came because Airi insisted.

24:45.130 --> 24:48.960
I refuse to become a
member of your idol group.

24:53.170 --> 24:54.469
Are you harassing me?

24:54.470 --> 24:56.880
No, I'm not.

24:57.230 --> 25:00.350
You're shining brightly in this video.

25:02.230 --> 25:03.239
Listen.

25:03.240 --> 25:08.979
I've never managed idols before,
so maybe I don't understand...

25:08.980 --> 25:14.860
but I don't think there are many people
who can make others happy, like this.

25:15.440 --> 25:16.440
So what?

25:16.750 --> 25:18.870
You're definitely one of them.

25:20.870 --> 25:24.729
Seeing this video, and watching you dance,

25:24.730 --> 25:28.610
somehow, encourages me to work harder.

25:29.180 --> 25:30.829
I don't know how to say this,

25:30.830 --> 25:36.709
but idols have the power
to give people courage.

25:36.710 --> 25:37.980
At least, I think they do.

25:38.780 --> 25:42.729
We want to make that kind of idol group,

25:42.730 --> 25:44.729
and we need you to do that.

25:44.730 --> 25:45.890
That's irrelevant.

25:46.900 --> 25:50.430
I know <i>I</i> don't have the power...

25:51.370 --> 25:53.280
to make others happy.

25:55.030 --> 25:59.230
I can't even make the people
around me, or myself happy.

25:59.740 --> 26:04.790
Encouraging and giving strength
to others is just unthinkable.

26:05.260 --> 26:06.429
Excuse me.

26:06.430 --> 26:07.430
Wait!

26:09.290 --> 26:11.670
See for yourself.

26:15.170 --> 26:16.680
Mayu.

26:17.050 --> 26:18.230
Sorry, Mayu.

26:19.640 --> 26:23.449
I thought it would make you more positive,

26:23.450 --> 26:25.629
but I shouldn't have interfered.

26:25.630 --> 26:26.689
I'm really sorry.

26:26.690 --> 26:28.480
It's fine, I'm not mad.

26:29.090 --> 26:32.530
But Matsuda-san... I mean, that manager...

26:33.200 --> 26:37.430
I don't think what he said is wrong.

26:37.960 --> 26:38.960
Um...

26:39.180 --> 26:40.280
Uh...

26:40.880 --> 26:44.500
I wish you would sing again, too.

26:45.680 --> 26:48.500
Sorry, but I can't.

27:02.470 --> 27:03.020
- Subject: Tokyo Dome!!!
- From:

27:02.470 --> 27:03.020
- Yoshikawa Megumi - Mayu! We're finally going to the Tokyo Dome! Our dream has
come true! I'm sorry we couldn't go together, but I'll sing for you! Megumi.

27:03.020 --> 27:05.520
- Yoshikawa Megumi - Mayu! We're finally going to the Tokyo Dome! Our dream has
come true! I'm sorry we couldn't go together, but I'll sing for you! Megumi.

27:03.023 --> 27:04.270
Subject: Tokyo Dome!!!

27:03.910 --> 27:06.549
<i>Mayu! We're finally
going to the Tokyo Dome!</i>

27:04.271 --> 27:05.520
From:

27:06.550 --> 27:08.129
<i>Our dream has come true!</i>

27:08.130 --> 27:10.829
<i>I'm sorry we couldn't go together,</i>

27:10.830 --> 27:13.269
<i>but I'll sing for you!</i>

27:13.270 --> 27:14.400
<i>Megumi.</i>

27:16.530 --> 27:18.759
<i>I'm going to talk to the President!</i>

27:18.760 --> 27:20.129
<i>It's no use.</i>

27:20.130 --> 27:22.279
<i>But this isn't fair...</i>

27:22.280 --> 27:24.779
<i>This isn't fair!</i>

27:24.780 --> 27:26.880
<i>Don't cry, Mayu.</i>

27:35.800 --> 27:35.960
New Message

27:35.800 --> 27:35.960
Yoshikawa Megumi

27:35.800 --> 27:35.920
Subject: Re: Tokyo Dome!!!

27:35.800 --> 27:35.878
Congratulations. You can do it!

27:36.669 --> 27:36.710
To:

27:36.720 --> 27:38.050
- New Message
- To:

27:36.720 --> 27:38.050
Yoshikawa Megumi

27:36.720 --> 27:37.090
Subject: Re: Tokyo Dome!!!

27:36.720 --> 27:38.050
Congratulations. You can do it!

27:37.090 --> 27:38.050
- Sending
- Subject: Re: Tokyo Dome!!!

27:40.010 --> 27:43.299
We're finally able to stand in
the place we've only dreamed of.

27:41.050 --> 27:46.310
Tokyo Dome Concert Press Conference

27:43.300 --> 27:46.310
However, instead of getting carried away,

27:46.810 --> 27:50.529
we'll focus on granting the numerous
wishes of our fans, and keep working hard

27:50.530 --> 27:53.820
in preparation for the
first day of the concert.

27:54.310 --> 27:58.689
I'm deeply honored to
stand amidst the idol world,

27:58.690 --> 28:00.400
the Tokyo Dome, in the center position.

28:01.070 --> 28:03.910
I promise it will be
our best performance yet.

28:04.880 --> 28:09.030
The Tokyo Dome has been
a big goal for the I-1 Club.

28:09.430 --> 28:14.209
However, now that it has become reality,
that goal becomes a stepping stone.

28:14.210 --> 28:16.840
The I-1 Club will set
their sights even higher...

28:14.500 --> 28:15.340
Grandpa.

28:15.341 --> 28:16.839
Oops.

28:16.840 --> 28:18.929
Huh? Where's Mom?

28:18.930 --> 28:21.330
She said she'd be late today.

28:21.730 --> 28:22.929
Is she working late?

28:22.930 --> 28:24.619
She's been working late a lot recently.

28:24.620 --> 28:25.850
You're right.

28:26.480 --> 28:29.230
Maybe she's trying not to
be too much of a sponge.

28:29.630 --> 28:30.580
Mayu...

28:30.581 --> 28:32.479
She's not a sponge.

28:32.480 --> 28:33.850
Thanks for the food.

28:35.280 --> 28:36.929
Welcome home.

28:36.930 --> 28:38.189
I'm home.

28:38.190 --> 28:39.579
You're early.

28:39.580 --> 28:41.279
I'll make you some dinner.

28:41.280 --> 28:42.429
I don't need any.

28:42.430 --> 28:43.870
I already ate.

28:44.480 --> 28:46.240
I told you I'd be late.

28:47.230 --> 28:49.130
You don't have to put it like that.

28:49.430 --> 28:51.219
Don't be so selfish.

28:51.220 --> 28:52.370
Mayu-chan...

28:52.870 --> 28:54.330
Selfish?

28:55.490 --> 28:57.380
Are you really one to talk?

29:02.730 --> 29:05.379
It really is such a
difficult world we live in.

29:05.380 --> 29:08.640
Everyone's always talking
about money, money, money.

29:08.960 --> 29:10.529
So, how was it?

29:10.530 --> 29:13.149
Well, I finally found someone.

29:13.150 --> 29:15.650
I decided to hire a local composer.

29:16.370 --> 29:20.329
I did want to ask a
successful idol songwriter,

29:20.330 --> 29:22.680
but I couldn't afford it.

29:23.160 --> 29:25.410
Isn't this how most ventures start out?

29:25.700 --> 29:28.079
So, how are the girls doing?

29:28.080 --> 29:32.909
They're doing voice and
dance training twice-weekly but...

29:32.910 --> 29:36.229
They're lacking in unity.

29:36.230 --> 29:38.279
Their singing abilities
are all over the place,

29:38.280 --> 29:40.630
and they feel nothing like a group.

29:43.480 --> 29:45.389
They lack cooperation.

29:45.390 --> 29:48.129
They're only thinking about themselves.

29:48.130 --> 29:50.930
Like each one only cares
about standing out on her own.

29:55.440 --> 29:57.879
They don't seem to be coming together.

29:57.880 --> 30:00.229
I see. I knew it.

30:00.230 --> 30:02.830
You knew it? Are you really okay with this?

30:03.380 --> 30:06.279
When they encounter an obstacle
they are unable to overcome separately,

30:06.280 --> 30:07.950
then they'll come together.

30:08.480 --> 30:10.329
When is that going to happen?

30:10.330 --> 30:12.079
It's already begun.

30:12.080 --> 30:12.580
Huh?

30:12.580 --> 30:14.685
October Schedule

30:12.580 --> 30:14.685
18 Fri Sendai Station (Afternoon)

30:12.580 --> 30:14.685
24 Thurs Sendai Station (Night)

30:12.580 --> 30:14.685
30 Wed Sendai Station (Night)

30:12.910 --> 30:14.629
Leave it to me, kid.

30:14.630 --> 30:16.790
This is what we prepared for.

30:14.686 --> 30:16.790
14 Mon Tsukasa-ya

30:14.686 --> 30:16.790
21 Mon Sendai Station (Night)

30:14.686 --> 30:16.790
27 Sun Sendai Station (Afternoon)

30:14.686 --> 30:16.790
Notice

30:18.300 --> 30:21.550
Mini-Concert

30:18.780 --> 30:21.540
Trials bring people together.

30:21.830 --> 30:25.359
Sorry. We normally use
this place for storage.

30:25.360 --> 30:30.129
I forgot to tell the delivery
men about your concert today.

30:30.130 --> 30:31.959
Can you do something about this?

30:31.960 --> 30:33.810
Well, we don't have
enough people right now.

30:35.650 --> 30:36.450
Kaya?

30:36.450 --> 30:37.380
There.

30:37.381 --> 30:39.439
So, where should I put this?

30:39.440 --> 30:41.029
Oh, thanks.

30:41.030 --> 30:42.030
Over here.

30:42.530 --> 30:43.579
Okay.

30:43.580 --> 30:44.980
I'll help, too.

30:45.330 --> 30:47.570
What? We're doing this?

30:47.930 --> 30:50.080
Let's get all of this out of the way.

30:50.630 --> 30:52.830
Now that we've...

30:54.330 --> 30:56.579
Is this how we're performing, leader?

30:56.580 --> 30:58.729
Well, it's a job...

30:58.730 --> 31:00.960
But even if we sing...

31:01.580 --> 31:02.779
Hello!

31:02.780 --> 31:04.529
We're Wake Up, Girls!

31:04.530 --> 31:07.680
Feel free to listen to our song!

31:07.980 --> 31:10.930
Uh... Please listen!

31:10.930 --> 31:13.459
I may say that, but I actually
really, really, love you!

31:13.460 --> 31:16.290
Shall we crawl? The wavering of life!

31:16.180 --> 31:18.079
I can't do this anymore!

31:18.080 --> 31:20.320
It's a complete waste of
time singing and dancing!

31:21.180 --> 31:22.929
It's our first performance.

31:22.930 --> 31:26.579
We don't have our own songs yet,
and we haven't even debuted properly.

31:26.580 --> 31:28.009
Matsuda-san's still not here?

31:28.010 --> 31:29.629
He's getting the car now.

31:29.630 --> 31:32.529
What? We haven't debuted yet?

31:32.530 --> 31:33.929
But we have a group name.

31:33.930 --> 31:37.040
It's not a group name. It's
the name of a love hotel.

31:37.350 --> 31:42.129
Normally, a debut is when
you release your first song.

31:42.130 --> 31:43.429
Really?

31:43.430 --> 31:47.459
They said we'd have a debut
song soon, but it's taking a while.

31:47.460 --> 31:49.049
I want to hurry up and sing.

31:49.050 --> 31:50.629
I'm exhausted.

31:50.630 --> 31:53.679
If it's always going to be
like this, there's no point.

31:53.680 --> 31:56.559
What? Nanami, you're going to quit?

31:56.560 --> 31:58.059
You're annoying.

31:58.060 --> 32:01.229
It can even be an indie label.

32:01.230 --> 32:02.879
If we don't debut, we won't get anywhere.

32:02.880 --> 32:05.629
Yeah, but I am a little disappointed.

32:05.630 --> 32:08.630
You're not as good as I thought you were.

32:09.080 --> 32:10.529
What do you mean, we're not good?

32:10.530 --> 32:12.079
Who cares?

32:12.080 --> 32:13.950
I'm hungry.

32:17.700 --> 32:19.199
Is the song ready?

32:19.200 --> 32:20.710
Of course it is.

32:20.659 --> 32:21.659
Debut Single

32:21.020 --> 32:22.249
Would you like to hear it?

32:22.250 --> 32:23.250
Yes!

32:26.470 --> 32:27.579
This song...

32:27.580 --> 32:28.709
It's enka...

32:28.710 --> 32:31.979
A man's life!

32:31.980 --> 32:33.549
Why is it an enka song?

32:33.550 --> 32:35.219
Well, because it was cheap.

32:35.220 --> 32:36.180
You don't like it?

32:36.181 --> 32:37.929
I made a new one.

32:37.481 --> 32:38.730
Green Leaves Entertainment

32:37.930 --> 32:38.930
How's this?

32:41.950 --> 32:42.979
This song...

32:42.980 --> 32:43.850
What is this?

32:43.851 --> 32:45.649
Die covered in blood!

32:45.650 --> 32:46.729
Kill!

32:46.730 --> 32:48.159
Please start taking this seriously!

32:48.160 --> 32:49.160
You don't like it?

32:49.950 --> 32:53.439
We still haven't come together yet.

32:53.440 --> 32:56.219
Everyone's got such a
strong sense of individuality.

32:56.220 --> 32:57.870
Individuality is important.

32:58.160 --> 32:59.160
You're right.

32:59.280 --> 33:02.559
In that respect, they're
all very interesting girls.

33:02.560 --> 33:04.049
Sounds fun.

33:04.050 --> 33:04.870
Huh?

33:04.871 --> 33:06.180
I guess.

33:06.830 --> 33:08.130
To tell the truth...

33:09.490 --> 33:11.530
It's supposed to be a secret,

33:11.850 --> 33:14.629
but maybe I'll tell you.

33:14.630 --> 33:15.890
Huh? What is it?

33:16.830 --> 33:21.079
At the end of the year, we're
going to release our debut CD.

33:21.080 --> 33:22.189
What? Really?

33:22.190 --> 33:23.779
It's an indie label, though.

33:23.780 --> 33:25.339
That's great, Airi!

33:25.340 --> 33:27.029
You're finally making your debut!

33:27.030 --> 33:28.030
Yeah!

33:33.030 --> 33:34.869
Good work, Twinkle.

33:34.870 --> 33:36.779
You wrote such a good song.

33:36.780 --> 33:39.879
You should've asked us in the first place.

33:39.880 --> 33:42.629
You made a group? They're cute.

33:42.630 --> 33:43.630
I suppose.

33:43.930 --> 33:46.329
Why did Twinkle write a song for us?

33:46.330 --> 33:48.279
The President is on good terms with them.

33:48.280 --> 33:49.230
Good terms?

33:49.231 --> 33:50.340
It means they're friends.

33:50.730 --> 33:54.179
Tange-san helped us
so much during our debut.

33:54.180 --> 33:56.139
We had to thank her somehow.

33:56.140 --> 33:59.779
With this song, we'll be
able to hold your debut event

33:59.780 --> 34:01.830
on the 20th of December at Macana!

34:03.380 --> 34:05.029
We don't have much time.

34:05.030 --> 34:05.880
You're right.

34:05.881 --> 34:08.729
What about our costumes?

34:08.730 --> 34:10.629
We haven't talked about that yet.

34:10.630 --> 34:11.630
President?

34:13.300 --> 34:13.990
President?

34:13.991 --> 34:15.660
Huh? What?

34:21.800 --> 34:22.870
Stop that!

34:29.150 --> 34:30.749
We're putting on our debut concert!

34:30.750 --> 34:33.030
Come check it out!

34:43.480 --> 34:46.629
I'm so nervous with the concert coming up.

34:46.630 --> 34:49.029
If you start getting nervous
now, you'll be in trouble.

34:49.030 --> 34:51.429
I've been working really hard.

34:51.430 --> 34:52.659
I know.

34:52.660 --> 34:54.649
I'm off to practise.

34:54.650 --> 34:55.929
You can do it.

34:55.930 --> 34:56.930
Yeah! Later.

35:28.830 --> 35:30.480
It's so cold.

35:31.130 --> 35:32.810
Good morning.

35:33.150 --> 35:33.240
- Stand Up!
- Stand Up!

35:36.530 --> 35:38.349
I wonder if they'll sell.

35:38.350 --> 35:41.450
We ended up making so many...

35:42.950 --> 35:45.780
Huh? The President's desk...

35:48.710 --> 35:51.085
My beloved darling is
having an emergency.

35:49.050 --> 35:51.729
<i>My beloved darling is having an emergency.</i>

35:51.086 --> 35:53.460
I'm leaving Sendai for a while.

35:51.730 --> 35:53.460
<i>I'm leaving Sendai for a while.</i>

35:54.430 --> 35:55.430
What?

35:58.630 --> 35:59.630
Yes.

36:00.030 --> 36:01.030
Yes.

36:01.630 --> 36:04.529
I'm still confirming the receipts.

36:04.530 --> 36:05.770
I'm sorry.

36:07.330 --> 36:09.730
As I thought, she didn't deposit the money.

36:07.751 --> 36:09.730
14 days until the concert!!

36:10.030 --> 36:11.180
You're kidding, right?

36:11.630 --> 36:14.240
The President would never do that, right?

36:14.680 --> 36:16.879
So she's disappeared, in other words?

36:16.880 --> 36:18.730
With all of our group's funds?

36:19.090 --> 36:21.739
Um... How are we going to...

36:21.740 --> 36:24.490
Is our concert going to be canceled?

36:24.800 --> 36:29.080
The CD's and concert
hall haven't been paid for.

36:29.400 --> 36:32.000
If we can't pay, we don't have any choice.

36:32.380 --> 36:33.779
But...

36:33.780 --> 36:35.280
In any case, we have no money.

36:37.630 --> 36:39.329
Ahh.

36:39.330 --> 36:41.139
We're being disbanded
right before our debut.

36:41.140 --> 36:43.759
This is a blow to my pride.

36:43.760 --> 36:46.010
I want to do the concert!

36:46.380 --> 36:47.759
I want to do it, too.

36:47.760 --> 36:50.269
Isn't there something we can do?

36:50.270 --> 36:52.020
I wish there was!

36:53.430 --> 36:54.480
Sorry.

36:55.680 --> 36:57.829
What have we been doing until now?

36:57.830 --> 37:00.280
I want back the time I've wasted.

37:02.130 --> 37:03.130
You're kidding.

37:03.630 --> 37:07.130
We've worked so hard,
but it's all for nothing.

37:07.730 --> 37:10.619
I don't want to believe
we've been deceived.

37:10.620 --> 37:13.380
After all, we worked so hard.

37:15.910 --> 37:16.910
But...

37:17.330 --> 37:18.510
This...

37:19.480 --> 37:20.920
This isn't fair!

37:21.710 --> 37:23.510
<i>This isn't fair!</i>

37:26.530 --> 37:29.630
I wonder if there really isn't a way.

37:44.440 --> 37:48.969
is my guide for today

37:48.970 --> 37:50.519
I love you

37:49.740 --> 37:51.329
I love you

37:50.520 --> 37:52.229
I really love you

37:51.330 --> 37:52.760
I really love you

37:52.230 --> 37:55.509
I love that I can tell you I love you

37:55.510 --> 37:57.109
I love you

37:57.110 --> 37:58.759
I really love you

37:58.760 --> 38:06.760
I am here, so I can say that

38:18.710 --> 38:25.569
We always make dreams come true

38:22.890 --> 38:25.610
Mayu-chan, where are you going?

38:25.570 --> 38:32.110
Yes! Yes! No one can stop us

38:37.120 --> 38:39.120
Aw, it's such a waste.

38:39.530 --> 38:41.279
There's nothing we can do.

38:41.280 --> 38:43.279
But we have outstanding payments.

38:43.280 --> 38:44.729
Should we try to sell them ourselves?

38:44.730 --> 38:48.260
Who would buy the CD of a group
that disbanded before it even debuted?

38:48.630 --> 38:51.799
I had you come here today
to discuss the CD's and

38:51.800 --> 38:54.010
what we should do going forward.

38:55.160 --> 38:59.629
Don't worry about the overstocked
CD's or any other outstanding payments.

38:59.630 --> 39:02.849
I'll handle it... somehow.

39:02.850 --> 39:03.949
Really?

39:03.950 --> 39:05.929
Uh... I really will handle it.

39:05.930 --> 39:07.680
You don't have to worry about it.

39:08.110 --> 39:11.909
But you've all worked so
hard on the debut concert...

39:11.910 --> 39:13.579
Is there any point?

39:13.580 --> 39:15.229
We can't debut anymore.

39:15.230 --> 39:17.329
A concert would just be a waste of time.

39:17.330 --> 39:18.230
Um...

39:18.231 --> 39:19.589
I agree, too.

39:19.590 --> 39:23.670
Instead of continuing to struggle,
we should think about our futures.

39:24.380 --> 39:25.150
Listen...

39:25.151 --> 39:26.779
Is this the end?

39:26.780 --> 39:28.320
We worked so hard.

39:28.680 --> 39:29.600
Listen...

39:29.600 --> 39:30.180
Listen!

39:30.180 --> 39:30.980
Huh?!

39:30.980 --> 39:31.980
What?

39:32.630 --> 39:36.280
We've made all sorts of
preparations and worked really hard.

39:36.970 --> 39:40.530
Even if it really is our last
performance, I still want to do it.

39:40.870 --> 39:42.830
I want to be an idol.

39:43.170 --> 39:45.900
Didn't you all want to become idols?

39:46.730 --> 39:48.160
Let's make our dreams come true!

39:52.010 --> 39:53.879
I want to do it!

39:53.880 --> 39:56.540
It was my dream! I want to do it!

39:57.480 --> 39:58.779
You're right.

39:58.780 --> 39:59.789
But...

39:59.790 --> 40:02.809
Why not? It's just once. I'll do it too.

40:02.810 --> 40:03.310
What?

40:03.311 --> 40:05.609
Leader, let's do it!

40:05.610 --> 40:07.300
Yeah, but...

40:14.800 --> 40:15.800
Mayu!

40:15.801 --> 40:17.810
Shimada Mayu...

40:19.160 --> 40:20.160
Um...

40:20.680 --> 40:22.820
Are you giving up on your concert?

40:23.230 --> 40:24.230
What?

40:24.270 --> 40:27.319
Well, we were just talking about it...

40:27.320 --> 40:28.820
You mustn't give up!

40:30.100 --> 40:32.570
If you give up, you'll regret it.

40:34.380 --> 40:36.930
I finally understand.

40:37.550 --> 40:39.710
I was lying to myself.

40:40.160 --> 40:41.960
Um... What are you talking about?

40:42.680 --> 40:45.830
I gave up on being an idol once.

40:46.280 --> 40:50.030
Since then, I've been
suppressing my feelings.

40:50.480 --> 40:55.340
I rejected my love of singing and dancing.

40:55.850 --> 40:58.600
I was afraid of being hurt again.

40:59.160 --> 41:03.269
But ever since the auditions
and my friend becoming an idol,

41:03.270 --> 41:07.829
watching her work made me
realize I wanted to be an idol too.

41:07.830 --> 41:08.830
Mayu...

41:08.860 --> 41:14.680
I've decided to believe in myself
again and become an idol once more.

41:15.160 --> 41:16.870
Please let me be an idol!

41:18.230 --> 41:19.649
I'm Shimada Mayu.

41:19.650 --> 41:22.819
Unlike everyone else, I haven't auditioned.

41:22.820 --> 41:26.380
But I came here because
I wanted to join the group.

41:26.860 --> 41:29.899
Please, let me join Wake Up, Girls!

41:29.900 --> 41:31.480
Please!

41:33.030 --> 41:33.830
You're kidding...

41:33.831 --> 41:35.879
<i>The</i> Shimada Mayu wants to join?

41:35.880 --> 41:36.979
All right!

41:36.980 --> 41:37.580
Wait!

41:37.580 --> 41:38.130
Huh?

41:38.131 --> 41:39.640
What do you think you're doing?

41:40.270 --> 41:42.729
I know a little of your past.

41:42.730 --> 41:44.389
You have my sympathy.

41:44.390 --> 41:49.629
But I don't think it's right to just
accept you into the group so easily.

41:49.630 --> 41:53.879
We haven't even decided if
we're going to continue working.

41:53.880 --> 41:57.630
I want to know if you're
prepared to handle that.

41:58.910 --> 42:02.420
I want to make myself happy.

42:02.700 --> 42:03.700
What?

42:04.130 --> 42:07.229
Everyone wants to make themselves happy.

42:07.230 --> 42:08.670
That's why you're here.

42:09.160 --> 42:12.780
No matter what challenges may await you,
that feeling never changes.

42:13.160 --> 42:14.330
I've realized that.

42:14.890 --> 42:17.029
I don't want to give up anymore.

42:17.030 --> 42:18.050
That's all.

42:20.140 --> 42:21.180
I see.

42:24.240 --> 42:25.490
You'll catch a cold.

42:25.950 --> 42:27.579
Come on! Let's do it.

42:27.580 --> 42:30.810
With you on our side,
I feel like it'll work out.

42:31.920 --> 42:35.399
You've been watching
us practice, haven't you?

42:35.400 --> 42:36.400
What?

42:37.450 --> 42:39.829
You looked like you wanted to join us.

42:39.830 --> 42:41.279
Come on, then.

42:41.280 --> 42:45.450
This may be our last performance,
but let's go out with a bang.

42:45.930 --> 42:47.079
Yeah!

42:47.080 --> 42:48.829
We're going to do it!

42:48.830 --> 42:50.179
All right!

42:50.180 --> 42:51.280
That's great!

42:51.281 --> 42:52.379
Huh? What's going on?

42:52.380 --> 42:53.529
Are we really doing it?

42:53.530 --> 42:54.679
Come on.

42:54.680 --> 42:56.970
We need to make a workable plan, though.

42:58.150 --> 43:00.469
I'll find a location for
the concert, somehow!

43:00.470 --> 43:02.129
What? Really?

43:02.130 --> 43:03.179
Leave it to me!

43:03.180 --> 43:06.230
If I can't at least do that, I'll
be a disgrace to the Date Clan!

43:13.490 --> 43:14.990
Student Metal Band Concert

43:18.740 --> 43:20.389
It's so cold!

43:20.390 --> 43:22.779
The Date Clan must
be rolling in their graves.

43:22.780 --> 43:25.719
We signed up at the last minute,
and we only have one song.

43:25.720 --> 43:26.979
I don't know about this.

43:26.980 --> 43:30.759
But we're the only ones here
that can score moe points!

43:30.760 --> 43:31.380
Moe?

43:31.380 --> 43:32.130
Moe!

43:32.390 --> 43:34.329
In any case, we get to perform.

43:34.330 --> 43:35.330
Let's do our best.

43:35.880 --> 43:37.579
Wake Up, Girls!

43:37.580 --> 43:41.449
We're holding our debut concert at 7:45pm!

43:41.450 --> 43:42.890
Check it out.

43:44.080 --> 43:45.260
This is...

43:47.020 --> 43:50.579
I'm shaking because
of the cold and anxiety.

43:50.580 --> 43:53.530
Look, my breath is so white.

43:54.770 --> 43:56.879
No one's here.

43:56.880 --> 43:58.429
Maybe it's too cold.

43:58.430 --> 44:00.629
Even if there's no one
here or it's too cold,

44:00.630 --> 44:01.829
we'll give it everything we've got.

44:01.830 --> 44:03.029
Isn't that what it means to be a pro?

44:03.030 --> 44:04.630
Right, Nanami?

44:05.630 --> 44:06.230
Huh?

44:06.231 --> 44:07.879
Are you cold? Nervous?

44:07.880 --> 44:08.889
Are you okay?

44:08.890 --> 44:10.290
I'm... fine...

44:10.630 --> 44:11.929
It's almost your turn.

44:11.930 --> 44:12.930
Get ready.

44:15.950 --> 44:17.550
You're all over the place.

44:18.050 --> 44:20.380
Sorry I couldn't get you costumes.

44:20.780 --> 44:22.300
That's fine, but...

44:24.230 --> 44:25.329
Oh, right.

44:25.330 --> 44:26.729
You need show-off panties.

44:26.730 --> 44:27.730
I'll go buy some.

44:27.810 --> 44:28.829
Who cares?

44:28.830 --> 44:29.440
What?

44:29.441 --> 44:31.749
It doesn't cost us anything
to show our underwear.

44:31.750 --> 44:33.619
Besides, there's not enough time.

44:33.620 --> 44:34.690
Let's get ready.

44:35.250 --> 44:37.999
Well, this is our first and last concert.

44:38.000 --> 44:40.079
We don't want to be stingy.

44:40.080 --> 44:41.949
It's a little extra
service for the audience.

44:41.950 --> 44:43.919
Nanami, can you do it?

44:43.920 --> 44:44.830
Yeah...

44:44.831 --> 44:46.659
I'm nervous, too.

44:46.660 --> 44:47.700
Relax, relax.

44:48.410 --> 44:49.700
Nanase-san.

44:55.210 --> 44:56.580
Come on, everyone.

45:01.980 --> 45:02.930
Um...

45:02.931 --> 45:03.989
Leader, lead the cheer.

45:03.990 --> 45:06.149
But I haven't thought of anything.

45:06.150 --> 45:07.729
How about "Let's do this"?

45:07.730 --> 45:12.629
When I say "Let's do this",
you say "Wake Up, Girls!"

45:12.630 --> 45:13.170
Okay.

45:13.170 --> 45:13.900
Sure.

45:13.900 --> 45:14.430
Okay.

45:14.430 --> 45:14.960
All right.

45:14.961 --> 45:16.230
Go ahead.

45:17.210 --> 45:18.479
Let's do it.

45:18.480 --> 45:20.770
Wake Up, Girls!

45:21.110 --> 45:23.620
SENDAI Student Metal Band Concert

45:27.670 --> 45:28.670
What?!

45:29.030 --> 45:30.030
Is that...

45:33.630 --> 45:38.640
Um, we're the Sendai-based
group, Wake Up, Girls!

45:38.980 --> 45:43.260
Um... This is our debut concert.

45:43.950 --> 45:47.179
We were allowed to participate
today at the very last minute.

45:47.180 --> 45:49.889
We still only have one song, but, um...

45:49.890 --> 45:51.800
We'll... um..

45:52.930 --> 45:54.390
We'll sing our hearts out.

45:54.820 --> 45:56.030
Please listen to our song.

46:23.670 --> 46:25.760
That's Shimada Mayu!

46:30.780 --> 46:36.480
Believing I could not dream

46:37.010 --> 46:43.119
I continued to protect
my small, quiet self.

46:43.120 --> 46:49.659
Even though this cruel
beginning hurt me badly,

46:49.660 --> 46:55.009
I was only afraid and
quickly turned my back.

46:55.010 --> 46:58.239
But I am who I am.

46:58.240 --> 47:01.549
No tricks will work against me.

47:01.550 --> 47:07.589
I decided I could only move
forward without giving up.

47:07.590 --> 47:13.250
Wake Up! Showered with sunshine.

47:14.060 --> 47:20.189
Right now, my heart's
hope is overlapping with you.

47:20.190 --> 47:25.849
Stand Up! There's no
night that doesn't end.

47:25.850 --> 47:32.159
So believe in smiles of tomorrow.

47:32.160 --> 47:38.750
Shine, my only one.

47:49.720 --> 47:55.999
I cried forever, I shouted forever.

47:56.000 --> 48:02.339
I continued to search
for my lost love forever.

48:02.340 --> 48:08.629
The moment I stood on the edge of despair,

48:08.630 --> 48:13.909
I heard the sound of a kind wind.

48:13.910 --> 48:17.189
Then I returned to discover.

48:17.190 --> 48:20.299
This is my stage.

48:20.300 --> 48:26.629
I fly into that sky once again.

48:26.630 --> 48:32.610
Wake Up! It opened my eyes.

48:32.870 --> 48:39.269
Because you don't want to cry anymore.

48:39.270 --> 48:44.779
Stand Up! The future lies ahead.

48:44.780 --> 48:51.059
That's why we depart right now.

48:51.060 --> 48:57.860
Watch me, my only one.

49:01.270 --> 49:07.129
More, more I want to tell you how I feel.

49:07.130 --> 49:14.009
There is something I can't give
up no matter how much I'm hurt.

49:14.010 --> 49:19.759
Listen, listen I'll sing my heart out.

49:19.760 --> 49:22.839
It's fine if they laugh at me.

49:22.840 --> 49:26.019
I won't lose.

49:26.020 --> 49:31.030
Stand up!

49:39.190 --> 49:45.230
Wake Up! Bathed in bright sunlight.

49:45.560 --> 49:51.799
The hope in my heart overlaps with you.

49:51.800 --> 49:57.409
Stand Up! There is no
night that doesn't end.

49:57.410 --> 50:03.790
Believe in tomorrow's smile.

50:04.480 --> 50:10.310
Wake Up! May my wish come true.

50:10.760 --> 50:17.089
I'm heading towards my
dream now, hands extending.

50:17.090 --> 50:22.729
Stand Up! Let's run without doubts.

50:22.730 --> 50:28.959
To live in this world.

50:28.960 --> 50:35.680
With you, my only one.

50:52.990 --> 50:54.870
We're finally at the Tokyo
Dome of our dreams!!

50:57.680 --> 51:00.879
We're finally here at the
Tokyo Dome of our dreams!

51:00.880 --> 51:02.280
Thank you!

51:03.780 --> 51:07.499
Everyone, do you love the I-1 Club?

51:07.500 --> 51:09.500
Yeah!

51:12.400 --> 51:14.229
Thank you very much!

51:14.230 --> 51:16.230
Thank you very much!

51:16.900 --> 51:19.760
Encore! Encore!

51:20.200 --> 51:23.230
Encore! Encore!

51:24.630 --> 51:26.179
Um, uh...

51:26.180 --> 51:29.879
We'd like to do an encore,
but we only have this one song...

51:29.880 --> 51:30.880
Okay!

51:32.280 --> 51:34.520
All right!

51:36.880 --> 51:38.859
What? An encore?!

51:38.860 --> 51:40.879
What are we supposed to do?

51:40.880 --> 51:44.370
What is the future of
Wake Up, Girls! and me?!

51:44.370 --> 51:46.370
The Seven Idols
